# SatQuery AI — Model 2: Cross-Modal Optical + SAR Fusion VQA

A single, self-contained Google Colab notebook that **creates paired Optical–SAR data, fine-tunes a dual-stream VLM with cross-modal feature fusion, evaluates, and saves everything to Google Drive**.

---

## Goal

Build a prototype cross-modal fusion VQA model that:
1. Accepts **two co-registered images** (Optical + SAR) of the **same geographic area** + a natural-language question.
2. **Fuses information from both sensors** at the feature level to produce a single, generative natural-language answer.
3. Trains on **~100 paired image sets** (each pair = 1 Optical + 1 SAR of the same scene).
4. Runs end-to-end on a **Google Colab T4 GPU** in a single session (~15–25 min training).

---

## How is this different from Model 1?

| Aspect | Model 1 (Single-Image VQA) | Model 2 (Cross-Modal Fusion) |
|--------|---------------------------|------------------------------|
| **Input** | 1 image (Optical OR SAR) | 2 images (Optical AND SAR, same area) |
| **Architecture** | Standard BLIP-2 (single image → LM) | **Dual-stream BLIP-2** (2 images → shared ViT/Q-Former → concatenate → LM) |
| **Visual tokens** | 32 query tokens from Q-Former | **64 query tokens** (32 optical + 32 SAR, concatenated) |
| **QA pairs** | Single-modality questions | **Cross-modal reasoning** ("What does the SAR tell you that the optical doesn't?") |
| **Key skill** | Scene description from one sensor | **Sensor fusion** — combining spectral & structural information |

