## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dual-Stream Architecture:** The core innovation is processing both images through BLIP-2's **shared frozen ViT + Q-Former** independently, then **concatenating the 32-token query outputs** from each stream into 64 visual tokens before projecting into the language model. This requires a lightweight custom `DualStreamBLIP2` wrapper class (~50 lines) that overrides the forward pass. The ViT and Q-Former weights remain **frozen and shared** — only the LoRA-adapted OPT language model sees the concatenated features.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Paired Dataset:** For the prototype, each "pair" comes from the same EuroSAT class. The optical image is a real Sentinel-2 patch from EuroSAT. The SAR image is synthesised from that same optical patch using calibrated speckle noise simulation (identical to Model 1's fallback). This guarantees co-registration for the prototype. For production, replace with real BigEarthNet-MM S1+S2 pairs.

